---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import WordCounter from '../components/WordCounter.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Free Word Counter Online — Count Words, Characters & More | WordCounterGo"
  description="WordCounterGo is a free, fast online word counter. Instantly count words, characters, sentences and paragraphs. Transform text with uppercase, lowercase, title case and more."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="hero-text">
        <h1 class="hero-title">Free Online <span class="accent">Word Counter</span></h1>
        <p class="hero-subtitle">Paste or type your text below. Word count, character count and reading time update instantly — no sign-up required.</p>
      </div>
      <WordCounter />
    </div>
  </section>

  <article class="content-section">
    <div class="container content-grid">
      <section class="content-block">
        <h2>What Is a Word Counter?</h2>
        <p>A word counter is an online tool that instantly analyses any piece of text and tells you exactly how many words, characters, sentences, and paragraphs it contains. Whether you are a student trying to hit an essay target, a blogger keeping posts within a certain length, or a professional copywriter watching your character count for social media, a word counter removes the guesswork and lets you focus on writing.</p>
        <p>WordCounterGo goes beyond basic counting. It also calculates your estimated reading time based on an average adult reading speed of 200 words per minute, so you know how long your audience will spend with your content before you hit publish.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="content-block">
        <h2>Why Use WordCounterGo?</h2>
        <p>There are dozens of word counters online, but most are cluttered with ads or require you to create an account. WordCounterGo is different: it is entirely free, requires no registration, and runs entirely in your browser. Your text never leaves your device — there is no server processing your words, which means complete privacy and near-instant results even on a slow connection.</p>
        <ul class="feature-list">
          <li><span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><span><strong>Real-time counting</strong> — every keystroke updates all stats live.</span></li>
          <li><span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><span><strong>Text transforms</strong> — switch between uppercase, lowercase, title case, and sentence case in one click.</span></li>
          <li><span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><span><strong>Clean spaces</strong> — remove double spaces and tidy up pasted text automatically.</span></li>
          <li><span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><span><strong>Privacy first</strong> — nothing is uploaded or stored. Ever.</span></li>
          <li><span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><span><strong>Mobile friendly</strong> — works perfectly on any screen size.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </section>
      <section class="content-block">
        <h2>How to Use the Word Counter</h2>
        <p>Using WordCounterGo takes seconds. Simply click inside the text box at the top of the page and start typing, or paste your existing text using <kbd>Ctrl+V</kbd> (Windows) or <kbd>Cmd+V</kbd> (Mac). The word count, character count, sentence count, paragraph count, and estimated reading time all update automatically as you type.</p>
        <p>Once your text is in the box, use the toolbar buttons to transform it:</p>
        <ul class="step-list">
          <li><strong>UPPERCASE</strong> — converts all letters to capitals.</li>
          <li><strong>lowercase</strong> — converts all letters to small case.</li>
          <li><strong>Title Case</strong> — capitalises the first letter of every major word.</li>
          <li><strong>Sentence case</strong> — capitalises only the first word of each sentence.</li>
          <li><strong>Clean spaces</strong> — removes extra whitespace and stray blank lines.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>When you are done, click <strong>Copy</strong> to copy the transformed text to your clipboard ready to paste anywhere.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="content-block">
        <h2>Word Count Goals by Content Type</h2>
        <p>Different types of writing have different ideal lengths. Here are some common benchmarks to keep in mind:</p>
        <ul class="feature-list">
          <li><span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">→</span><span><strong>Tweet / X post:</strong> up to 280 characters.</span></li>
          <li><span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">→</span><span><strong>LinkedIn post:</strong> 150–300 words for best engagement.</span></li>
          <li><span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">→</span><span><strong>Blog post:</strong> 1,000–2,500 words for SEO and readability.</span></li>
          <li><span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">→</span><span><strong>Academic essay:</strong> typically 500, 1,000, or 2,500 words as set by the institution.</span></li>
          <li><span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">→</span><span><strong>Short story:</strong> 1,000–7,500 words.</span></li>
          <li><span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">→</span><span><strong>Novel:</strong> 70,000–100,000 words on average.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </section>
      <section class="content-block">
        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        <div class="faq">
          <div class="faq-item"><h3>Is WordCounterGo free to use?</h3><p>Yes, completely free. There is no premium tier, no account required, and no hidden costs. Just open the page and start counting.</p></div>
          <div class="faq-item"><h3>Does my text get saved or shared?</h3><p>No. WordCounterGo runs entirely in your browser using JavaScript. Your text is never sent to any server, stored in any database, or shared with anyone. When you close the tab, it is gone.</p></div>
          <div class="faq-item"><h3>How is reading time calculated?</h3><p>Reading time is estimated at 200 words per minute, which reflects the average silent reading speed of an adult. The figure is rounded up to the nearest minute so you always have a comfortable buffer.</p></div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .hero { padding: 2.5rem 0 0; }
  .hero-text { text-align: center; margin-bottom: 1.75rem; }
  .hero-title { font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.5rem); font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.15; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .accent { color: var(--color-green); }
  .hero-subtitle { font-size: var(--text-lg); color: var(--text-secondary); max-width: 560px; margin: 0 auto; line-height: 1.6; }
  .content-section { padding: 3.5rem 0; }
  .content-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 2.5rem; max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .content-block { background-color: var(--bg-surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); box-shadow: var(--shadow-card); padding: 1.75rem 2rem; transition: background-color var(--transition), border-color var(--transition); }
  .content-block h2 { font-size: var(--text-2xl); font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-primary); margin-bottom: 1rem; line-height: 1.2; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent); padding-bottom: 0.5rem; display: inline-block; }
  .content-block p { font-size: var(--text-base); color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.75; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .content-block p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .feature-list { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.625rem; margin-top: 0.75rem; }
  .feature-list li { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.625rem; font-size: var(--text-base); color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.6; }
  .feature-icon { flex-shrink: 0; color: var(--accent); font-weight: 700; margin-top: 1px; }
  .step-list { margin: 0.75rem 0 1rem; padding-left: 1.25rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.375rem; }
  .step-list li { font-size: var(--text-base); color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.6; list-style-type: disc; }
  .faq { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.25rem; }
  .faq-item { border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); padding-left: 1rem; }
  .faq-item h3 { font-size: var(--text-base); font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary); margin-bottom: 0.375rem; line-height: 1.4; }
  .faq-item p { font-size: var(--text-base); color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 0 !important; }
  kbd { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 6px; font-family: inherit; font-size: 0.8em; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary); background-color: var(--bg-page); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-sm); box-shadow: 0 1px 0 var(--border); }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { .content-block { padding: 1.25rem 1rem; } .hero { padding-top: 1.75rem; } }
</style>
